[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	NoSQL
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	Azure Cosmos DB is a NoSQL (Not only SQL) database, which means it can handle unstructured, semi-structured, structured, and vector data types. 
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	Vector database
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	Azure Cosmos DB is a vector database that can handle large-scale vector data. 
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	Multiple APIs
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	Azure Cosmos DB offers multiple database APIs, including NoSQL, MongoDB, PostgreSQL, Cassandra, Gremlin, and Table. 
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	Physical partitions
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	The underlying storage mechanism for data in Azure Cosmos DB is called a physical partition. 
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	Logical partitions
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	Azure Cosmos DB abstracts the partitioning concept with a logical partition. 
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	Built-in vector search
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	Azure Cosmos DB offers built-in vector search to query vectors and relevant data efficiently. 
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	SLA-backed availability
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	Azure Cosmos DB offers SLA-backed 99.999 percent availability for NoSQL data. 
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	Serverless or autoscale options
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	Azure Cosmos DB offers serverless or autoscale options to pay for only what you use. 
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	Azure Cosmos DB is designed to provide:
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	High availability
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	Scalability
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	Low-latency access to data
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	Single-digit millisecond response times
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	Automatic and instant scalability
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	Guaranteed speed at any scale
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	Elastic throughput and storage scaling across any number of geographical regions')
