[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	 - Outage Information - 
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	Here is the information about the outage on Amazon AWS:
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	**Outage Details:**
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	* **Services Impacted:** Amazon CloudWatch Logs, Amazon Data Firehose, Amazon Elastic Container Service (ECS), AWS Lambda, Amazon Redshift, and AWS Glue
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	* **Regions Affected:** Northern Virginia (US-EAST-1) Region
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	* **Availability Zones Affected:** Not specified
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	**Root Cause of Outage:**
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	The outage was caused by a degradation of one of the internally-used cells of the Amazon Kinesis Data Streams service.
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	**Duration of Outage:**
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	* **Start Time:** 2:45 PM PDT
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	* **End Time:** 9:37 PM PDT
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	* **Duration:** 7 hours and 52 minutes
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	* **Days:** 1 day
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	**Downtime Period:**
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	The outage started at 2:45 PM PDT on July 30th, 2024, and lasted for approximately 8 hours.
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	**Resolution Time:**
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	Normal operations were restored to the Kinesis Data Streams cell by 7:21 PM PDT, which marked the end of the outage. The backlog of delayed S3 events completed processing at 2:38 AM PDT on August 1st.
